ons, bootlegging, corruption, drug trafficking, extortion, fencing, fraud, hijacking, illegal gambling, loan-sharking, money laundering, murder, pier thefts, pornography, prostitution, racketeering, and waste management violations.", "rerank_score": -1.2805}, {"title": "Sam DeCavalcante", "text": "Simone Rizzo \"Sam\" DeCavalcante (March 3, 1912 \u2013 February 7, 1997), known as \"Sam the Plumber\", was a member of the New Jersey Mafia.  Claiming descent from the Italian royal family, DeCavalcante was nicknamed \"The Count\".  The Kefauver hearings later named his crime family the DeCavalcante crime family since he was the boss of the family current to those hearings.", "rerank_score": -2.2372}], "candidate_answer": "Park Dietz", "source": "gold", "generator": "gold", "difficulty": "trivial", "transformation": null, "expected_label_hint": "SUPPORTED", "corpus_size": 12}
