eras composed by Richard Wagner.  He created Pogner in \"Die Meistersinger von N\u00fcrnberg\" (June 21, 1868), Fafner in \"Das Rheingold\" (September 22, 1869), Hunding in \"Die Walk\u00fcre\" (June 26, 1870), and Harald in \"Die Feen\" (June 29, 1888).", "rerank_score": 0.2561}, {"title": "Adolf Robinson", "text": "Adolf Robinson (1838\u20131920) was an Austrian baritone who had a major opera career during the second half of the 19th century.  His extensive stage repertoire contained numerous Wagnerian roles such as Wotan in \"The Ring Cycle\" and Hans Sachs in \"Die Meistersinger von N\u00fcrnberg\".  Other highlights of his career included the title characters in Rossini's \"William Tell\", Mozart's \"Don Giovanni\", Verdi's \"Rigoletto\", H\u00e9rold's \"Zampa\", and Heinrich Marschner's \"Der Templer und die J\u00fcdin\".", "rerank_score": -0.1177}], "candidate_answer": "opera", "source": "gold", "generator": "gold", "difficulty": "trivial", "transformation": null, "expected_label_hint": "SUPPORTED", "corpus_size": 17}
