ction of being the first #1 song on \"Billboard\" magazine's then-newly created Hot 100 chart.  He recorded 19 additional Top 10 hits and was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame on January 21, 1987.", "rerank_score": -1.8776}, {"title": "Ricky Nelson", "text": "Eric Hilliard Nelson (May 8, 1940 \u2013 December 31, 1985) was an American actor, musician, and singer-songwriter.  From age eight he starred alongside his family in the radio and television series \"The Adventures of Ozzie and Harriet\".  In 1957 he began a long and successful career as a popular recording artist.", "rerank_score": -2.1764}], "candidate_answer": "Tom Wopat", "source": "gold", "generator": "gold", "difficulty": "trivial", "transformation": null, "expected_label_hint": "SUPPORTED", "corpus_size": 24}
