\".", "rerank_score": 0.206}, {"title": "Albert Johnson (gridiron football)", "text": "Albert Johnson III (born November 11, 1977 in Houston, Texas) is a Canadian Football League player for the Winnipeg Blue Bombers.  Johnson played his college football for Southern Methodist University and then signed with the Saskatchewan Roughriders where he played three games in 1999.  Johnson then signed with the Blue Bombers and went on to win the league's Rookie of the Year Award in 2000 after leading the league in return yardage.", "rerank_score": -1.2131}], "candidate_answer": "Prodigy", "source": "gold", "generator": "gold", "difficulty": "trivial", "transformation": null, "expected_label_hint": "SUPPORTED", "corpus_size": 13}
