sed in 1803, with text additions made by the composer.  In the 2010s, it stands as one of the most performed symphonies in the world.", "rerank_score": 1.4911}, {"title": "Symphony No. 9 (Beethoven)", "text": "The Symphony No. 9 in D minor, Op.  125, is the final complete symphony composed from 1822 to 1824 by the German composer Ludwig van Beethoven.  It was first performed in Vienna on 7 May 1824.", "rerank_score": 0.6868}], "candidate_answer": "Ottokar Kernstock", "source": "gold", "generator": "gold", "difficulty": "trivial", "transformation": null, "expected_label_hint": "SUPPORTED", "corpus_size": 21}
