l a large and intense hurricane when the storm made landfall near Port O'Connor, Texas.", "rerank_score": -2.7214}, {"title": "Hurricane Edith (1971)", "text": "Hurricane Edith was the strongest hurricane to form during the 1971 Atlantic hurricane season and the southernmost landfalling Category 5 hurricane on record in the Atlantic until surpassed by Hurricane Felix of 2007.  Edith developed from a tropical wave on September 5 and quickly strengthened into a hurricane in the Caribbean Sea.  Edith rapidly intensified on September 9 and made landfall on Cape Gracias a Dios as a Category 5 hurricane on the Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Scale.", "rerank_score": -2.7292}], "candidate_answer": "Hurricane Ivan", "source": "gold", "generator": "gold", "difficulty": "trivial", "transformation": null, "expected_label_hint": "SUPPORTED", "corpus_size": 24}
